  "notes": "So So Def's ballad harmonist — the research calls him \"the richest chord vocabulary on the Atlanta board\", 1998–2010. The spine is \"**55–73 half-time** ballads (reads 110–147) plus 96–110 straight\", so the felt band is the base with the mode at 73, the sourced tempo of the fully-transcribed record in D minor. Three drum deltas, all subtractive: \"a single kick on 1 plus one on the 8th before 3\" (one or two hits, syncopation 0.08, `lockTo808` 0.4 for the \"TR-808-styled kick/hat pair\"), \"clap layered with snare on beat 3\", and \"16th hats only under the chorus\" at 0.15 fill density with `rolls.freqPerBar` 0 and `fills` at sixteen bars, because the entry says \"No fills, no rolls\" in as many words. The identifying parameter is the harmony and the research gives it whole: \"**6- and 7-chord cycles**, e.g. `i–VI–VII–i–iv–VII–V7` (Dm–B♭maj7–C–Dm–Gm7–C–A7) in D minor at 73 BPM, with maj7/m7/add9 extensions and a real V7 cadence\". That seven-numeral cycle is the top-weighted family, `maxChords` is 7 — the largest in this section — the triad share is 0.1 and ninth is 0.38; the numerals carry degree only, with the sevenths expressed in `extensions` as the schema requires. \"He plays the instruments himself; Johntá Austin writes lyric and melody over the finished track\" is why the melody is authored conservatively and the counter is a `sustain_pad`-led string layer at +12 — his string arrangements are documented as handed to Ron Fair. The low end is \"soft 808-derived sub on chord roots with a short slide into the downbeat, mixed under the piano\", so a bass part with a 0.32 `glideProb` and no `drums.bass808` block. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED; the research gives progression, key, tempo and division of labour, not a programmed kit.",
